00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:54.860
black hole can drive jets that extend tens of thousands of light years, far beyond the scale

00:06:54.860 --> 00:07:00.500
of an entire galaxy disk. If you could ride one of those jets outward from the Galactic Center,

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:06.340
You would first encounter gas heated to millions of degrees by shockwaves, then see that material

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:09.200
cool and form new structures along the jet path.

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:15.080
In Messier 106, the jets have created two extra arms of glowing gas that sit at right

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:17.000
angles to the normal spiral arms.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:23.300
Chandra X-ray observations show these arms glow in royal blue because the gas reaches temperatures

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:24.900
hot enough to emit X-rays.

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:30.320
The jets themselves move at a substantial fraction of the speed of light, carrying energy

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:35.600
equivalent to the output of millions of ordinary stars, yet astronomers still cannot explain

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:41.440
exactly why some black holes launch steady, powerful jets, while others remain quiet despite

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:47.200
similar masses and accretion rates. We can map the jets and measure the heated gas, but

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:53.120
the trigger that decides whether a jet forms remains unknown. Before we go, keep an eye on the

